# HTTPS is mandatory: a PWA will not install without it and push will not work (docs/12).
# DOMAIN is where the app lives. DOMAIN_ALIASES (optional, space-separated) get certificates too.
#
# On an alias, a page a browser opens is sent on to DOMAIN, so new installs happen on one origin.
# Everything else (the API, the service worker, scripts, photos) is still served there: an app
# installed on an old address draws its pages from its service worker and never reaches the redirect,
# and a cross-origin redirect would break its API calls (no CORS) and its updates (a service worker
# script may not redirect). Such an app keeps working, with its own sign-in and notifications, and
# it updates. The redirect stays temporary while the main domain can still change
# (sslip.io → ubite.hypha.ro → ubite.acc.unibuc.ro).
{$DOMAIN} {$DOMAIN_ALIASES} {
	@alias_page {
		not host {$DOMAIN}
		header Sec-Fetch-Mode navigate
	}
	# Browsers that send no fetch metadata: a GET that asks for HTML.
	@alias_page_legacy {
		not host {$DOMAIN}
		method GET HEAD
		header !Sec-Fetch-Mode
		header Accept *text/html*
	}
	redir @alias_page https://{$DOMAIN}{uri}
	redir @alias_page_legacy https://{$DOMAIN}{uri}
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy app:8080
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		-Server
	}
}
